      <workList xml:id="idm71">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e223220">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_901979cb">A4:001</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_e6353014" xml:lang="it">Adagio – Allegro</title>
            <title type="uniform" xml:id="title_e7ce883d" xml:lang="en">Sonata for organ</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_8889e496">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_a58d4234">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_4daad615">
               <p xml:id="idm80">Most often the first folio of Scheibe's finished works were signed and dated. The present, possibly incomplete organ work does not include a date or a signature suggesting that Scheibe did not finish it (that is, it is a working copy) – a conclusion supported by the numerous additions, changes and cancellations which Scheibe made during the compositional process. The work was most likely acquired through G.J.D. <persName xml:id="idm81" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Poelchau</persName>'s acquaintances in Copenhagen (<persName xml:id="idm82" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">C.E.F. Weyse</persName>?), presumably connected to the estate of Scheibe.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_ace53bf9">
               <language xml:id="en">English</language>
               <language xml:id="it">Italian</language>
            </langUsage>
