            </titleStmt>
            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_c6d1301c">
               <extent xml:id="extent_7980249f">1 bifolio</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_214eb1e7">34.5x21.5</dimensions>
               <watermark xml:id="watermark_ad0fc2cd">paper with watermark though not visible (containing unidentifiable letters or digits); edges very worn and thin paper of an inferior quality.</watermark>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_f871ad50">In 2<rend xml:id="idm38" rend="sup">o</rend>; upright format; music (fols. 1r–2r), a work by <persName xml:id="idm39" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Baldassare Galuppi</persName> in a foreign but professional hand (fol. 2v) which is also found in one of Scheibe's cantatas of 1747 (SchW B2:432); in all a single bifolio. 'Allegro' on fol. 4v might also be in Scheibe's hand. Hand-ruled paper, 18 staves (9 mm; single rastrum used) in light ink and music in dark brown ink; at the bottom of fol. 2r, an extra stave has been added. The source is Scheibe's working copy rather than a fair copy as it includes several changes, cancellations and additions in ink. The source might be incomplete lacking other movements.</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
